# Rust
/target
**/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock
# ...except the application/tool lockfiles, which are committed so builds are
# reproducible. CI runs these with `--locked`, which fails outright when the
# lockfile is missing.
!engine/Cargo.lock
!tools/artifact-manifest/Cargo.lock

# Build outputs
*.aar
*.apk
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log
logs/

.claude/
.worktrees/

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Node (if used for tooling)
node_modules/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Android
*.iml
.gradle/
local.properties
/build
/captures
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# Temporary
*.tmp
*.temp
AI_PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md

!docs/

# Python bytecode from the packaging scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Staged Linux SDK package (scripts/build-linux-sdk.sh output)
dist/

# V8 archives for every ABI are build products, not source. None are tracked:
# they were what exhausted the repo's LFS quota and took CI down. Each is
# reproduced by scripts/build-v8-<os>.sh, described by the committed
# component-manifest.json beside it, and fetched in CI by
# scripts/fetch-v8-archives.sh, which verifies the sha256 that manifest records.
engine/third_party/rusty_v8/*/librusty_v8.a
engine/third_party/rusty_v8/x86_64-linux-gnu/librusty_v8.a

# Windows V8 build products of scripts/build-v8-windows.sh, same policy as the
# Linux archive above (the ~190 MB .lib and its generated binding are not
# tracked; the script reproduces them). Ignoring the whole dir also stops a
# stray `git add -A` from committing a 190 MB library into LFS.
engine/third_party/rusty_v8/x86_64-pc-windows-msvc/

# Binaries built by the out-of-tree consumer examples. They are proof the
# package works, not source; examples/c-host/build-with-pkgconfig.sh and the
# CMake project regenerate them.
examples/c-host/linux/c-host
examples/c-host/linux/c-host-cmake

# Screenshots dropped in the repo root are scratch, not project content.
Snipaste_*.png

# Android example build outputs
examples/c-host/android/build/
examples/c-host/android/.cxx/
examples/c-host/android/src/main/jniLibs-static/
examples/c-host/linux/c-host

# Maintainer working notes, internal planning documents and one-off audit
# tooling. These are deliberately not published: they are the accumulated
# record of which trap was hit on which device and how each was resolved,
# which is the expensive half of this project to rebuild and is worth nothing
# to someone consuming the runtime. What a consumer needs is README.md,
# docs/BUILD.md, docs/multiplatform-architecture.md and include/migo/.
# Placed last so these win over the `!docs/` re-inclusion above.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.codex/
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/
docs/gtm-*.md
platforms/windows/SPIKE-REPORT.md
tools/wx-api-diff/

# Local-only operational notes (`*.local.md`). Same policy as the working
# notes above: they are for the maintainer's machine, not for consumers.
*.local.md
